[
 {
  "section": "THE QUESTION",
  "start": 0.0
 },
 {
  "text": "Right now, almost one in every six people on Earth lives in India.",
  "section": "THE QUESTION",
  "start": 0.0,
  "end": 2.602,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "That's about 1.46 billion people.",
  "section": "THE QUESTION",
  "start": 3.052,
  "end": 4.694,
  "pause_after": 0.85
 },
 {
  "text": "Now imagine only one in forty did.",
  "section": "THE QUESTION",
  "start": 5.544,
  "end": 6.867,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Same country.",
  "section": "THE QUESTION",
  "start": 7.317,
  "end": 8.121,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "Same rivers.",
  "section": "THE QUESTION",
  "start": 8.371,
  "end": 9.107,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "Same borders.",
  "section": "THE QUESTION",
  "start": 9.357,
  "end": 10.151,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "Just 200 million people instead.",
  "section": "THE QUESTION",
  "start": 10.401,
  "end": 11.775,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "Would life be calmer?",
  "section": "THE QUESTION",
  "start": 12.025,
  "end": 13.007,
  "pause_after": 0.8
 },
 {
  "text": "Would everyone be richer?",
  "section": "THE QUESTION",
  "start": 13.807,
  "end": 14.863,
  "pause_after": 0.8
 },
 {
  "text": "Would the trains finally be empty?",
  "section": "THE QUESTION",
  "start": 15.663,
  "end": 17.051,
  "pause_after": 0.8
 },
 {
  "text": "The answer is more surprising than you'd think.",
  "section": "THE QUESTION",
  "start": 17.851,
  "end": 19.394,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Let's find out.",
  "section": "THE QUESTION",
  "start": 19.844,
  "end": 20.624,
  "pause_after": 1.6
 },
 {
  "section": "THE RULES",
  "start": 22.224
 },
 {
  "text": "First, the rules.",
  "section": "THE RULES",
  "start": 22.224,
  "end": 23.07,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "Nobody disappears.",
  "section": "THE RULES",
  "start": 23.32,
  "end": 24.298,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "Nothing terrible happens.",
  "section": "THE RULES",
  "start": 24.548,
  "end": 25.771,
  "pause_after": 0.65
 },
 {
  "text": "Instead, India's population simply stopped growing, long ago, at around 200 million.",
  "section": "THE RULES",
  "start": 26.421,
  "end": 30.114,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "For comparison, India had about 238 million people back in 1901.",
  "section": "THE RULES",
  "start": 30.564,
  "end": 34.369,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Everything else stays the same: the land, the rivers, the monsoon, the borders.",
  "section": "THE RULES",
  "start": 34.819,
  "end": 37.817,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "So what changes?",
  "section": "THE RULES",
  "start": 38.267,
  "end": 39.205,
  "pause_after": 1.6
 },
 {
  "section": "SPACE",
  "start": 40.805
 },
 {
  "text": "Start with space.",
  "section": "SPACE",
  "start": 40.805,
  "end": 41.605,
  "pause_after": 0.65
 },
 {
  "text": "Today, India has about 490 people for every square kilometre.",
  "section": "SPACE",
  "start": 42.255,
  "end": 45.405,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "At 200 million, that drops to about 67.",
  "section": "SPACE",
  "start": 45.855,
  "end": 47.729,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "That's roughly the same as Mexico today.",
  "section": "SPACE",
  "start": 48.179,
  "end": 49.508,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Now think about an ordinary morning.",
  "section": "SPACE",
  "start": 49.958,
  "end": 51.225,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Mumbai packs in around 20,000 people per square kilometre.",
  "section": "SPACE",
  "start": 51.675,
  "end": 54.276,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Packed trains.",
  "section": "SPACE",
  "start": 54.726,
  "end": 55.455,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "Packed buses.",
  "section": "SPACE",
  "start": 55.705,
  "end": 56.448,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "Packed classrooms.",
  "section": "SPACE",
  "start": 56.698,
  "end": 57.596,
  "pause_after": 0.65
 },
 {
  "text": "In a 200 million India, the same morning looks different.",
  "section": "SPACE",
  "start": 58.246,
  "end": 60.551,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "A seat on the train.",
  "section": "SPACE",
  "start": 61.001,
  "end": 61.736,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "A shorter queue at the school gate.",
  "section": "SPACE",
  "start": 62.186,
  "end": 63.27,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "A flat with a spare room.",
  "section": "SPACE",
  "start": 63.721,
  "end": 64.531,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Cities would likely be smaller, with more space between the buildings.",
  "section": "SPACE",
  "start": 64.981,
  "end": 67.496,
  "pause_after": 0.85
 },
 {
  "text": "But there's a catch.",
  "section": "SPACE",
  "start": 68.346,
  "end": 69.17,
  "pause_after": 0.65
 },
 {
  "text": "Fewer people also means fewer taxpayers to build and run the railways, the roads and the schools, across the same enormous country.",
  "section": "SPACE",
  "start": 69.82,
  "end": 75.588,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Luckily, there's more room.",
  "section": "SPACE",
  "start": 76.038,
  "end": 77.066,
  "pause_after": 0.65
 },
 {
  "text": "Unluckily, there's less money to fill it.",
  "section": "SPACE",
  "start": 77.716,
  "end": 78.934,
  "pause_after": 1.6
 },
 {
  "section": "WATER, LAND AND AIR",
  "start": 80.534
 },
 {
  "text": "Now, the things you can't make more of: water, land and food.",
  "section": "WATER, LAND AND AIR",
  "start": 80.534,
  "end": 82.918,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Official figures put India at roughly 1,500 cubic metres of water per person each year.",
  "section": "WATER, LAND AND AIR",
  "start": 83.368,
  "end": 87.408,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Below 1,700 counts as water stressed.",
  "section": "WATER, LAND AND AIR",
  "start": 87.858,
  "end": 89.662,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "With about seven times fewer people sharing the same rivers and groundwater, each person would have about seven times as much.",
  "section": "WATER, LAND AND AIR",
  "start": 90.112,
  "end": 95.109,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "More farmland per person.",
  "section": "WATER, LAND AND AIR",
  "start": 95.559,
  "end": 96.754,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "Less pressure on forests.",
  "section": "WATER, LAND AND AIR",
  "start": 97.004,
  "end": 98.2,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "Fewer vehicles and factories.",
  "section": "WATER, LAND AND AIR",
  "start": 98.45,
  "end": 99.837,
  "pause_after": 0.85
 },
 {
  "text": "But pollution isn't only about how many people there are.",
  "section": "WATER, LAND AND AIR",
  "start": 100.687,
  "end": 102.744,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "It's about how they live.",
  "section": "WATER, LAND AND AIR",
  "start": 103.194,
  "end": 104.033,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "A smaller, richer India might drive more cars and use more electricity per person.",
  "section": "WATER, LAND AND AIR",
  "start": 104.483,
  "end": 107.984,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Fewer people don't automatically mean cleaner air.",
  "section": "WATER, LAND AND AIR",
  "start": 108.434,
  "end": 110.18,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "They just change the maths.",
  "section": "WATER, LAND AND AIR",
  "start": 110.63,
  "end": 111.58,
  "pause_after": 1.6
 },
 {
  "section": "FARMS AND FOOD",
  "start": 113.18
 },
 {
  "text": "Farms are a good place to see it.",
  "section": "FARMS AND FOOD",
  "start": 113.18,
  "end": 114.206,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "In 1970, the average farm in India was about 2.3 hectares.",
  "section": "FARMS AND FOOD",
  "start": 114.656,
  "end": 117.858,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "By 2015, it had shrunk to about 1.08.",
  "section": "FARMS AND FOOD",
  "start": 118.308,
  "end": 120.538,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Why?",
  "section": "FARMS AND FOOD",
  "start": 120.988,
  "end": 121.437,
  "pause_after": 0.8
 },
 {
  "text": "Land gets divided as families grow.",
  "section": "FARMS AND FOOD",
  "start": 122.237,
  "end": 123.562,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Today, around 86 percent of Indian farms are smaller than two hectares.",
  "section": "FARMS AND FOOD",
  "start": 124.012,
  "end": 127.256,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "In a country whose population stopped growing, farms would be split far less often.",
  "section": "FARMS AND FOOD",
  "start": 127.706,
  "end": 130.974,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Bigger farms.",
  "section": "FARMS AND FOOD",
  "start": 131.424,
  "end": 132.151,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "More machines per field.",
  "section": "FARMS AND FOOD",
  "start": 132.401,
  "end": 133.498,
  "pause_after": 0.65
 },
 {
  "text": "Maybe higher earnings for each farmer.",
  "section": "FARMS AND FOOD",
  "start": 134.148,
  "end": 135.392,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Maybe.",
  "section": "FARMS AND FOOD",
  "start": 135.842,
  "end": 136.39,
  "pause_after": 0.65
 },
 {
  "text": "A bigger farm isn't automatically a better one.",
  "section": "FARMS AND FOOD",
  "start": 137.04,
  "end": 138.678,
  "pause_after": 0.85
 },
 {
  "text": "But a farmer with more land and fewer people to share it with starts from a stronger place.",
  "section": "FARMS AND FOOD",
  "start": 139.528,
  "end": 142.877,
  "pause_after": 1.6
 },
 {
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 144.477
 },
 {
  "text": "Now, the money question.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 144.477,
  "end": 145.552,
  "pause_after": 0.65
 },
 {
  "text": "India's economy is worth about 4.3 trillion dollars a year.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 146.202,
  "end": 149.075,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Divide that by 1.46 billion people, and you get roughly 2,800 dollars each.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 149.525,
  "end": 153.711,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Now divide the same economy by 200 million.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 154.161,
  "end": 156.079,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "That's about 21,500 dollars each.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 156.529,
  "end": 158.188,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "More than seven times richer.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 158.438,
  "end": 159.471,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "Sounds perfect, right?",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 159.721,
  "end": 160.723,
  "pause_after": 0.8
 },
 {
  "text": "Here's the trap.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 161.523,
  "end": 162.244,
  "pause_after": 0.65
 },
 {
  "text": "The economy wouldn't stay the same size.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 162.894,
  "end": 164.354,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "An economy isn't a pie that gets sliced thinner.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 164.804,
  "end": 166.563,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "It's made by people.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 167.013,
  "end": 167.982,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "Workers.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 168.232,
  "end": 168.818,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "Customers.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 169.068,
  "end": 169.694,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "Engineers.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 169.944,
  "end": 170.641,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "Farmers.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 170.891,
  "end": 171.481,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "Shop owners.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 171.731,
  "end": 172.478,
  "pause_after": 0.65
 },
 {
  "text": "Take most of them away, and you don't just have fewer mouths.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 173.128,
  "end": 175.443,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "You have far fewer hands, and far fewer buyers.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 175.893,
  "end": 177.689,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "India's median age is about 29.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 178.138,
  "end": 179.829,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "In the United States, it's about 39.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 180.279,
  "end": 181.72,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "In China, about 40.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 182.17,
  "end": 183.33,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "That's an enormous young workforce.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 183.58,
  "end": 184.699,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "A 200 million India would have a smaller market, a smaller workforce, and less weight in the world.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 185.149,
  "end": 189.245,
  "pause_after": 0.85
 },
 {
  "text": "So would people be richer?",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 190.095,
  "end": 191.187,
  "pause_after": 0.8
 },
 {
  "text": "Maybe.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 191.987,
  "end": 192.535,
  "pause_after": 0.65
 },
 {
  "text": "It depends on whether the economy shrinks faster than the population.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 193.185,
  "end": 195.57,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "History has both: small countries that are very rich, and small countries that are very poor.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 196.02,
  "end": 199.564,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Size alone doesn't decide it.",
  "section": "THE MONEY QUESTION",
  "start": 200.014,
  "end": 200.987,
  "pause_after": 1.6
 },
 {
  "section": "JOBS",
  "start": 202.587
 },
 {
  "text": "Now the part that worries economists most: jobs.",
  "section": "JOBS",
  "start": 202.587,
  "end": 204.529,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Every year, millions of young Indians reach working age and look for work.",
  "section": "JOBS",
  "start": 204.979,
  "end": 207.895,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Estimates of how many new jobs India needs each year range from about 8 million to over 20 million, depending on who's counting.",
  "section": "JOBS",
  "start": 208.345,
  "end": 213.998,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Creating that many jobs, year after year, is one of the hardest problems the country faces.",
  "section": "JOBS",
  "start": 214.448,
  "end": 218.138,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "In a 200 million India, far fewer young people would arrive each year.",
  "section": "JOBS",
  "start": 218.588,
  "end": 221.613,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Less competition for each job.",
  "section": "JOBS",
  "start": 222.063,
  "end": 223.246,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "Wages might rise.",
  "section": "JOBS",
  "start": 223.496,
  "end": 224.488,
  "pause_after": 0.85
 },
 {
  "text": "But there's a catch.",
  "section": "JOBS",
  "start": 225.338,
  "end": 226.162,
  "pause_after": 0.65
 },
 {
  "text": "Fewer people also means fewer customers to hire for, fewer new businesses, and fewer ideas.",
  "section": "JOBS",
  "start": 226.812,
  "end": 230.94,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Jobs aren't a fixed number.",
  "section": "JOBS",
  "start": 231.39,
  "end": 232.4,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "They're created by demand, and demand comes from people.",
  "section": "JOBS",
  "start": 232.85,
  "end": 234.898,
  "pause_after": 1.6
 },
 {
  "section": "MORE PEOPLE, MORE IDEAS",
  "start": 236.498
 },
 {
  "text": "Here's a deeper reason a big population matters.",
  "section": "MORE PEOPLE, MORE IDEAS",
  "start": 236.498,
  "end": 238.281,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Economists have long argued that ideas work differently from everything else.",
  "section": "MORE PEOPLE, MORE IDEAS",
  "start": 238.731,
  "end": 241.773,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "If you eat a meal, nobody else can eat it.",
  "section": "MORE PEOPLE, MORE IDEAS",
  "start": 242.223,
  "end": 243.669,
  "pause_after": 0.85
 },
 {
  "text": "But if someone invents a better engine, or a new way to farm, everyone can use it at once.",
  "section": "MORE PEOPLE, MORE IDEAS",
  "start": 244.519,
  "end": 248.146,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "That insight helped earn economist Paul Romer a share of the 2018 Nobel Prize.",
  "section": "MORE PEOPLE, MORE IDEAS",
  "start": 248.596,
  "end": 252.348,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "In many economic models, more people means more minds working on problems, and every good idea can be shared with all of them.",
  "section": "MORE PEOPLE, MORE IDEAS",
  "start": 252.798,
  "end": 257.824,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "A 200 million India would still have plenty of talented people.",
  "section": "MORE PEOPLE, MORE IDEAS",
  "start": 258.274,
  "end": 260.869,
  "pause_after": 0.85
 },
 {
  "text": "But it would have far fewer of them.",
  "section": "MORE PEOPLE, MORE IDEAS",
  "start": 261.719,
  "end": 262.847,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Fewer scientists.",
  "section": "MORE PEOPLE, MORE IDEAS",
  "start": 263.297,
  "end": 264.173,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "Fewer engineers.",
  "section": "MORE PEOPLE, MORE IDEAS",
  "start": 264.423,
  "end": 265.295,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "Fewer founders.",
  "section": "MORE PEOPLE, MORE IDEAS",
  "start": 265.545,
  "end": 266.366,
  "pause_after": 0.65
 },
 {
  "text": "Progress isn't only about how much you have.",
  "section": "MORE PEOPLE, MORE IDEAS",
  "start": 267.016,
  "end": 268.615,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "It's about how many people are finding ways to do more with it.",
  "section": "MORE PEOPLE, MORE IDEAS",
  "start": 269.065,
  "end": 271.114,
  "pause_after": 1.6
 },
 {
  "section": "A SMALLER GIANT",
  "start": 272.714
 },
 {
  "text": "There's a way to check this.",
  "section": "A SMALLER GIANT",
  "start": 272.714,
  "end": 273.537,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Countries of around 200 million people already exist.",
  "section": "A SMALLER GIANT",
  "start": 273.987,
  "end": 276.435,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Brazil, Nigeria and Pakistan each have well over 200 million.",
  "section": "A SMALLER GIANT",
  "start": 276.885,
  "end": 279.901,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "A 200 million India would still rank among the ten biggest countries on Earth.",
  "section": "A SMALLER GIANT",
  "start": 280.351,
  "end": 283.493,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "That's what most people miss.",
  "section": "A SMALLER GIANT",
  "start": 283.943,
  "end": 284.861,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "It wouldn't be a small country.",
  "section": "A SMALLER GIANT",
  "start": 285.311,
  "end": 286.348,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "It would just be a smaller giant.",
  "section": "A SMALLER GIANT",
  "start": 286.798,
  "end": 287.99,
  "pause_after": 1.6
 },
 {
  "section": "THE SLOWDOWN",
  "start": 289.59
 },
 {
  "text": "Here's something that surprises people.",
  "section": "THE SLOWDOWN",
  "start": 289.59,
  "end": 290.806,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "India's population is already slowing down.",
  "section": "THE SLOWDOWN",
  "start": 291.256,
  "end": 292.888,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "According to the UN, the average Indian woman now has about 1.9 children, below the 2.1 needed to keep a population steady.",
  "section": "THE SLOWDOWN",
  "start": 293.338,
  "end": 299.321,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Growth continues for now, because so many people are young and still starting families.",
  "section": "THE SLOWDOWN",
  "start": 299.771,
  "end": 303.157,
  "pause_after": 0.85
 },
 {
  "text": "But the UN expects India to peak at about 1.7 billion in the early 2060s, and then begin to fall.",
  "section": "THE SLOWDOWN",
  "start": 304.007,
  "end": 309.126,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "So the real question isn't whether India's population will stop growing.",
  "section": "THE SLOWDOWN",
  "start": 309.576,
  "end": 312.35,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "It's when, how fast, and what the country looks like when it does.",
  "section": "THE SLOWDOWN",
  "start": 312.8,
  "end": 315.051,
  "pause_after": 1.6
 },
 {
  "section": "FIFTY YEARS LATER",
  "start": 316.651
 },
 {
  "text": "Now fast-forward fifty years.",
  "section": "FIFTY YEARS LATER",
  "start": 316.651,
  "end": 318.143,
  "pause_after": 0.65
 },
 {
  "text": "A country that stops growing early also ages early.",
  "section": "FIFTY YEARS LATER",
  "start": 318.793,
  "end": 320.856,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Fewer young people supporting more older people, sooner.",
  "section": "FIFTY YEARS LATER",
  "start": 321.306,
  "end": 323.188,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "So the real India faces the pressure of more people.",
  "section": "FIFTY YEARS LATER",
  "start": 323.638,
  "end": 325.657,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "A 200 million India would face the pressure of fewer.",
  "section": "FIFTY YEARS LATER",
  "start": 326.107,
  "end": 328.175,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Neither is easy.",
  "section": "FIFTY YEARS LATER",
  "start": 328.625,
  "end": 329.502,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "They're just different problems.",
  "section": "FIFTY YEARS LATER",
  "start": 329.752,
  "end": 331.005,
  "pause_after": 1.6
 },
 {
  "section": "TWO MORNINGS",
  "start": 332.605
 },
 {
  "text": "Picture two children walking to school in the same city.",
  "section": "TWO MORNINGS",
  "start": 332.605,
  "end": 334.509,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "In today's India, she squeezes onto a crowded bus and sits in a full classroom.",
  "section": "TWO MORNINGS",
  "start": 334.959,
  "end": 338.196,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "In a 200 million India, she probably gets a seat, and a smaller class.",
  "section": "TWO MORNINGS",
  "start": 338.646,
  "end": 341.67,
  "pause_after": 0.85
 },
 {
  "text": "But her school might be further away, because fewer children means fewer schools.",
  "section": "TWO MORNINGS",
  "start": 342.52,
  "end": 345.488,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "And her parents might earn less, because the economy around them is smaller.",
  "section": "TWO MORNINGS",
  "start": 345.938,
  "end": 348.588,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Same child.",
  "section": "TWO MORNINGS",
  "start": 349.038,
  "end": 349.75,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "Same city.",
  "section": "TWO MORNINGS",
  "start": 350.0,
  "end": 350.705,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "Different trade-offs.",
  "section": "TWO MORNINGS",
  "start": 350.955,
  "end": 351.847,
  "pause_after": 0.25
 },
 {
  "text": "Nobody wins everything.",
  "section": "TWO MORNINGS",
  "start": 352.097,
  "end": 353.241,
  "pause_after": 1.6
 },
 {
  "section": "THE REAL ANSWER",
  "start": 354.841
 },
 {
  "text": "So, would India be better off with 200 million people?",
  "section": "THE REAL ANSWER",
  "start": 354.841,
  "end": 357.654,
  "pause_after": 0.8
 },
 {
  "text": "Not automatically.",
  "section": "THE REAL ANSWER",
  "start": 358.454,
  "end": 359.311,
  "pause_after": 0.65
 },
 {
  "text": "More space, more water, shorter queues.",
  "section": "THE REAL ANSWER",
  "start": 359.961,
  "end": 361.416,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Yes.",
  "section": "THE REAL ANSWER",
  "start": 361.866,
  "end": 362.315,
  "pause_after": 0.85
 },
 {
  "text": "But also fewer workers, a smaller market, and a smaller voice in the world.",
  "section": "THE REAL ANSWER",
  "start": 363.165,
  "end": 366.224,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "A big population is a strain.",
  "section": "THE REAL ANSWER",
  "start": 366.674,
  "end": 367.776,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "It's also a strength.",
  "section": "THE REAL ANSWER",
  "start": 368.226,
  "end": 369.123,
  "pause_after": 0.65
 },
 {
  "text": "The real lesson isn't about a number.",
  "section": "THE REAL ANSWER",
  "start": 369.773,
  "end": 371.093,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "It's about what a country does with the people it has.",
  "section": "THE REAL ANSWER",
  "start": 371.543,
  "end": 373.293,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Right now, one in six humans lives in India.",
  "section": "THE REAL ANSWER",
  "start": 373.743,
  "end": 375.423,
  "pause_after": 0.45
 },
 {
  "text": "Would you want one in forty?",
  "section": "THE REAL ANSWER",
  "start": 375.873,
  "end": 376.974,
  "pause_after": 2.5
 }
]